  "body": "The maintainer said on 2026-11-20, in the discussion of #2949 (folders as the only source of the machine and post lists):\n\n> Well in this case we need to be able to load mch and cps files from users disk\n\nNow (main at 13f26da99):\n- In the browser build the button \"Load machine (.mch)\" is greyed with the reason \"needs a file picker\" (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/browser_files.rs`, test `a_file_button_is_greyed_with_its_reason_in_the_browser`).\n- The file drop (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/file_drop.rs`) takes only model files: `stl`, `obj`, `step`, `stp` and `sc`.\n- A post file (`.cps`) has no browser path at all.\n- The browser build has no disk. Once #2949 removes the compiled-in copy, the browser needs another way to get a user's own machine or post file.\n\nWanted:\n- The browser build loads a `.mch` file and a `.cps` file that the user picks or drops. It uses the existing commands (`LoadMachineFile`, `SelectPostFile`), so it is undoable and the MCP tool is the same. The bytes come from the browser, not from a path.\n- A folder picker (`<input webkitdirectory>`) loads all `.mch` and `.cps` files of one folder, read-only, in one step. It works in Chrome, Firefox and Safari. The File System Access API is not needed.\n- The file drop accepts `.mch` and `.cps` files, and several files at once, with each file refused by name and reason if it does not parse. A bad file does not change the project.\n- A loaded file shows in the machine list and the post list as a user entry for the session. A saved project that names it by file name gives a refusal by name when the file is not loaded (#2319), not a silent fallback.\n- The browser can keep the files for the next session (IndexedDB) if the maintainer wants it. This is a separate decision: put the options in the decision file.\n\nDone means: in the browser build, a picked or dropped `.mch` and `.cps` file is in the lists and a document posts with it. A malformed file is refused by name. A structural test (AccessKit label, role, enabled state) pins each button. The button \"Load machine (.mch)\" is no longer greyed in the browser.\n\nRelated: #2949 (folders only), #2282 (closed), #2414 (merged), #1437 (browser downloads).\n",
